undo --all no longer prints a ✓ or tells the model it deleted files that are still there. Committed as 129e77e5; build, all tests, clippy and fmt pass.

What changed in `handle_undo_all_in`:
• Which files count as deleted: after git clean -fd, the code checks the disk for each untracked file instead of trusting git's exit code. A file only counts as deleted if it is really gone.
• The last line: ✓ reverted all uncommitted changes only appears when no untracked file survived. Otherwise it prints, in yellow: ⚠ partially reverted: tracked changes reverted; 1 untracked file could not be removed: locked/f.
• What the model is told: only files that are really gone are listed as deleted X (was untracked). Survivors go in a separate note listing each one as NOT removed: X (git clean failed or left it). I kept them out of the main list so its "reverted N files" count stays right. I also changed the suggested (git clean failed) wording, because the same check catches a file that git clean skips without failing.
• Exit code: still 1 when git fails (#1058).
• Turn history: still cleared on a partial revert. The comment explains why: tracked files were reset, so the per-turn snapshots no longer match the working tree.
• When `checkout` fails: this already stopped before claiming anything. A test now drives that branch: a modified tracked file in a read-only (555) directory made git fail with unable to unlink old 'd/x'. So I didn't need to file a separate issue for it.

Tests are in src/commands_git_undo_tests.rs. Both read-only-directory setups first check that the directory really refuses writes, and skip if it doesn't (for example, when running as root). On this runner both really made git fail. A test with nothing locked confirms the old ✓ path and the model's note are exactly as before. As a positive control I forced every file to count as deleted: exactly the git-clean-failure test went red, and the restore was done in the same command.

Other changes:
• src/commands_git.rs went from 3753 to 3809 lines, all production code. Its row in tests/module_size.rs is updated with the reason.
• docs/src/usage/commands.md has one new sentence describing the partial-revert line.
